                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had a lot of fun with this game! The basic idea is much the same as the original ReThink, there are lasers to redirect, combine, split, and block. But there are also fresh elements like cubes, antigravity fields and more!\n\nIt was very interesting to try the Rethink formula in a more freeform way, and I think that it will appeal more to the vast majority of players than the original ReThink. The increase in freedom (less built-in restrictions) made the game much more of a think outside the box game rather than the more cold hard logic of the original. It also made the game MUCH easier in my opinion. Despite a similar amount of puzzle rooms, this one took me half the time of the original ReThink, but mileage may vary of course.\n\nI highly recommend this one if you are into the classic 1st person puzzle games like Portal and especially Talos Principle.",
